language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session2_maximal_independent_sets: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ An independent set of a graph is a set of nodes no two of which are adjacent, and it is maximal when no other node can be added to it. Find a maximal independent set of the graph whose adjacency is given: for each node, the set of its adjacent nodes.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `session2_maximal_independent_sets.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session2_maximal_independent_sets.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `session2_maximal_independent_sets_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py session2_maximal_independent_sets.json
$   savilerow model.eprime session2_maximal_independent_sets_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the number of nodes, numbered 1 to n
given n : int(1..)
$ adjacency_list_dim1: the number of nodes (derived by the converter from the data; equals n)
given adjacency_list_dim1 : int(1..)
$ adjacency_list_dim2: the number of adjacent nodes listed per node (derived by the converter from the data)
given adjacency_list_dim2 : int(1..)
$ adjacency_list_len[i]: the number of nodes adjacent to node i (derived by the converter from the data; not a field of the reader's JSON)
given adjacency_list_len : matrix indexed by [int(1..adjacency_list_dim1)] of int(0..adjacency_list_dim2)
$ adjacency_list[i,k]: the k-th node adjacent to node i (1-based node numbers), for k up to adjacency_list_len[i]; later entries are padding 0
given adjacency_list : matrix indexed by [int(1..adjacency_list_dim1), int(1..adjacency_list_dim2)] of int(0..n)

$ nodes[i]: node i is in the maximal independent set
find nodes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of bool

such that
$ no two nodes of the set are adjacent: if node i is in the set, none of its adjacent nodes is
forAll i : int(1..n) . forAll k : int(1..adjacency_list_len[i]) . (nodes[i] -> !nodes[adjacency_list[i,k]]),
$ maximality: every node not in the set is adjacent to a node that is in the set, so no node can be added
forAll i : int(1..n) . (nodes[i] \/ (exists k : int(1..adjacency_list_len[i]) . nodes[adjacency_list[i,k]]))
